  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 22-layer alternating ZnS/MgF2 thin-film stack on CaF2 substrate under air incidence. Initialize all layer thicknesses to a quasi-periodic schedule centered at 1050 nm with bounds [750, 1250] nm. Implement two-phase optimization: Phase 1 jointly optimizes adjacent layer pairs (d_i, d_{i+1}) for i=1,3,5,...,21 to preserve local optical phase continuity; Phase 2 decouples all 22 layers for fine-grained thickness tuning. Target: maximize mean transmittance in passbands [3250-3350 nm, 4200-4300 nm] and minimize mean transmittance in stopbands [2500-3100 nm, 4450-5000 nm]. Use coherent TMM solver with normal unpolarized illumination. Output thicknesses_nm array, best_target_score, valid_candidates count, and tightest_margin. Topology realization override: disregard any symbolic repeat count, range, or ellipsis above and use exactly 6 alternating ZnS/MgF2 pairs (12 finite layers). Optimize only continuous physical thicknesses; the task compiler must fully expand every finite layer. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 2500-3100 nm, 3250-3350 nm, 4200-4300 nm, 4450-5000 nm. soft objectives: High transmittance in 3.25-3.35 um and 4.20-4.30 um bands; Low transmittance in 2.50-3.10 um and 4.45-5.00 um bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: High transmittance in 2.50-3.10 um and 4.45-5.00 um bands. manufacturing constraints: Total layer count <= 24; No metal layers; Conventional depositable infrared inorganic dielectric materials only.",
